WEBVTT

00:11.010 --> 00:15.223
[theme music playing]

01:33.635 --> 01:37.847
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:43.019 --> 01:43.937
[Marcille] No.

01:44.020 --> 01:46.189
-[gasps]
-Falin…

01:46.272 --> 01:49.400
Can she even be revived after all that?

01:50.068 --> 01:52.445
I've heard
that it's been done before, but…

01:53.404 --> 01:56.366
-[grunts]
-Hey, Laios. What are you--

01:56.449 --> 01:57.992
[Laios] The resurrection office.

01:58.076 --> 01:59.744
They'll know what to do.

02:00.328 --> 02:02.288
Are you planning to take everything?

02:02.372 --> 02:04.874
But aren't Warg bones mixed in there too?

02:04.958 --> 02:06.584
[Laios] It's hard to tell them apart.

02:06.668 --> 02:08.002
-Mm.
-[Senshi sighs]

02:08.086 --> 02:09.504
[Chilchuck] Let me help.

02:09.587 --> 02:11.756
[whimpers, gasps]

02:11.840 --> 02:14.008
-Please wait!
-[both gasp]

02:14.092 --> 02:17.137
The link between the soul and body
is fragile now.

02:17.220 --> 02:18.763
You shouldn't move her.

02:19.305 --> 02:23.017
[Marcille] <i>The more damaged the body is,
the weaker the soul's bond.</i>

02:23.101 --> 02:24.519
<i>When a resurrection fails,</i>

02:24.602 --> 02:27.605
<i>it's usually
because the soul separated too far,</i>

02:27.689 --> 02:30.275
<i>or because the body wasn't fully restored.</i>

02:30.358 --> 02:31.901
[Laios] Then, what should we do?

02:32.569 --> 02:36.030
We go get a revival specialist
and revive her here.

02:36.614 --> 02:38.116
[Marcille] <i>But the restoration requires</i>

02:38.199 --> 02:41.119
<i>more than twice the amount of calories
for the damaged parts.</i>

02:41.202 --> 02:45.039
<i>So, we'd also need to bring
a lot of fresh meat for it to work.</i>

02:45.123 --> 02:47.250
It would rot on the way down, wouldn't it?

02:47.333 --> 02:48.835
-Hang on.
-Huh?

02:48.918 --> 02:49.919
[Marcille] Yes.

02:50.003 --> 02:53.882
We have a large amount of fresh meat
right here in front of us.

02:54.757 --> 02:56.426
Hey. Now hold on a sec.

02:56.509 --> 02:59.304
You're gonna resurrect her
with dragon meat?

02:59.387 --> 03:02.015
Reviving isn't even your specialty.

03:03.391 --> 03:06.394
I didn't want to scare anyone
so I never mentioned it.

03:07.437 --> 03:09.063
What I specialize in

03:09.147 --> 03:12.525
is actually ancient magic,
which is highly forbidden.

03:13.067 --> 03:16.195
Its use is frowned upon,
but using it to revive Falin…

03:16.779 --> 03:18.197
is our best option.

03:18.281 --> 03:20.283
-Marcille!
-Black magic?

03:20.366 --> 03:21.951
That stuff is evil!

03:22.619 --> 03:24.913
-Magic doesn't have morality.
-[Chilchuck gasps]

03:27.165 --> 03:29.709
Well, Laios? It's your choice.

03:30.418 --> 03:31.961
Please do it, Marcille.

03:32.045 --> 03:34.505
Bring my sister back from the dead.

03:36.549 --> 03:37.759
All right, then.

03:37.842 --> 03:38.968
I'll try.

03:39.052 --> 03:40.595
[Chilchuck] Are you guys insane?

03:40.678 --> 03:42.931
Using dragon meat of all things!

03:43.014 --> 03:45.600
Goat and pig are what people
would normally use for this.

03:45.683 --> 03:47.560
But we don't have that right now.

03:47.644 --> 03:49.103
[Laios] All right, let's start.

03:50.021 --> 03:51.356
Mm.

03:51.439 --> 03:52.649
[Marcille inhales deeply]

03:53.900 --> 03:55.360
-[blood squelches]
-[both groan]

04:02.450 --> 04:03.743
First things first,

04:03.826 --> 04:06.704
I would like to put the body
back in its original shape,

04:06.788 --> 04:08.873
so I'll start assembling her skeleton.

04:08.957 --> 04:10.416
That makes sense.

04:10.500 --> 04:12.627
I'm familiar with canine skeletons.

04:12.710 --> 04:15.505
[Laios] So I'll work
on putting the Wargs together.

04:17.257 --> 04:18.174
[both] Mm.

04:18.258 --> 04:20.385
That's kinda unnecessary, isn't it?

04:20.468 --> 04:23.721
Not if it helps us avoid mixing something
and making dumb mistakes!

04:23.805 --> 04:25.390
-Mm.
-Mm.

04:25.473 --> 04:28.226
[Marcille] Humans have around 200 bones.

04:28.309 --> 04:31.813
[Laios] Then we're looking
at about 840 bones total.

04:31.896 --> 04:33.898
[Chilchuck] Huh? How do you know that?

04:34.607 --> 04:36.609
[Laios] Dogs have around 320 bones,

04:36.693 --> 04:39.320
and there are two skulls here,
so it's easy math.

04:39.904 --> 04:42.407
Let's start
with the most recognizable ones.

04:42.991 --> 04:45.368
[Marcille]
The rounder set is a human's rib cage.

04:45.451 --> 04:48.329
And the spine
is directly connected to the ribs.

04:48.413 --> 04:51.666
Their curves don't look the same,
so they're easy to tell apart.

04:51.749 --> 04:53.835
[Marcille] The toughest ones
are the smaller bones

04:53.918 --> 04:55.503
from the hands and feet.

04:55.586 --> 04:58.256
[Laios] Yeah, it's a lot harder
to tell the difference.

04:58.756 --> 05:01.676
Let's start with the bigger pieces
and work down.

05:01.759 --> 05:05.054
This piece that I'm holding
is the ankle bone.

05:05.138 --> 05:08.683
Find the next biggest one,
then connect the two sides that line up,

05:09.350 --> 05:11.269
and the instep is complete.

05:12.353 --> 05:14.647
And then,
we have the bones from the hands.

05:14.731 --> 05:16.941
Let's arrange them
starting with the fingers.

05:17.025 --> 05:18.943
I got it! Ha!

05:19.527 --> 05:21.195
[Laios] Like this, right?

05:21.279 --> 05:22.947
-So close.
-[Laios] Aw.

05:23.031 --> 05:26.075
Actually, the longest metacarpal,
despite what you might think,

05:26.159 --> 05:27.452
goes on the pointer finger.

05:28.161 --> 05:31.706
That just leaves us with the ones
that connect the fingers to the wrist.

05:32.707 --> 05:34.208
[Laios] Hmm.

05:35.543 --> 05:36.961
Hmm…

05:37.045 --> 05:39.756
-Hint, please!
-This isn't a game, Laios!

05:41.799 --> 05:44.469
[sighs] There.

05:44.552 --> 05:46.012
[Marcille] It's ready!

05:46.095 --> 05:48.473
THE BONE STRUCTURES
OF FALIN AND WARGS

05:49.390 --> 05:50.725
How do I put this?

05:51.726 --> 05:53.478
What a beautiful skeleton.

05:53.561 --> 05:55.396
[Chilchuck] Not bad for some bones.

05:55.480 --> 05:57.690
[Senshi] Seems she had
a good calcium intake.

05:58.441 --> 06:00.985
[Chilchuck] This isn't gonna revive
the Wargs too, is it?

06:01.069 --> 06:03.988
Only human souls get bound to the dungeon.

06:04.072 --> 06:08.034
Because otherwise, this place would burst
from all the monsters' souls.

06:08.576 --> 06:14.248
[foreboding music playing]

06:18.961 --> 06:21.339
All right, here we go.

06:21.422 --> 06:22.757
[grunts]

06:23.591 --> 06:24.759
[Marcille] <i>O Pilitsham.</i>

06:25.384 --> 06:27.887
<i>O Esdoms. O Villaru.</i>

06:28.721 --> 06:31.390
<i>Casuszameo Rotokt Artumcuks.</i>

06:32.100 --> 06:34.268
-<i>O Kunquikeo. Eoktum Kome.</i>
-[gasps]

06:35.728 --> 06:41.275
[Marcille] <i>Tumao Elm Finktow Kemesfo.
Aoewauk Aentujon.</i>

06:41.359 --> 06:44.237
<i>Tumao Elm Finktow Kemesfo.</i>

06:44.320 --> 06:46.864
<i>Aoewauk Aentujon.</i>

06:47.365 --> 06:50.034
<i>Tumao Elm Finktow Kemesfo.</i>

06:50.701 --> 06:54.288
<i>Aoewauk Aentujon…</i>

06:55.706 --> 06:56.707
[Laios] Marcille!

06:57.625 --> 06:59.043
[gasps]

06:59.127 --> 07:00.920
She just fainted.

07:01.003 --> 07:02.547
[Chilchuck] So, what happened?

07:02.630 --> 07:04.173
Did it actually work?

07:05.508 --> 07:07.093
Huh?

07:10.763 --> 07:12.306
[whimpers softly]

07:20.022 --> 07:21.482
[gasps]

07:21.566 --> 07:22.900
[coughs]

07:22.984 --> 07:23.985
Falin!

07:24.861 --> 07:26.779
Her airway's full of blood!

07:26.863 --> 07:28.781
[Laios] All right, just cough it out.

07:28.865 --> 07:29.949
[Falin coughs, retches]

07:30.032 --> 07:31.659
[Laios] There. All good.

07:31.742 --> 07:33.286
[Falin coughs, retches]

07:34.537 --> 07:36.164
[Falin coughing]

07:36.247 --> 07:37.290
Falin.

07:40.626 --> 07:44.255
[pants]

07:47.383 --> 07:49.051
[Falin faintly] Brother…

07:52.722 --> 07:54.223
[in normal voice] I'm glad you're safe.

07:56.976 --> 07:58.561
-You're cold.
-[gasps]

07:58.644 --> 08:00.730
[Laios] Right, my armor! Sorry!

08:00.813 --> 08:02.398
Let me go get you some clothes.

08:02.982 --> 08:04.066
Huh?

08:05.026 --> 08:07.111
[Laios] Falin, what's the matter?

08:07.778 --> 08:09.530
You're feeling okay, right?

08:09.614 --> 08:11.073
[Falin] Uh-huh.

08:11.157 --> 08:12.700
Good. I'm glad to hear it.

08:13.284 --> 08:14.660
-[Laios] Marcille.
-[groans]

08:14.744 --> 08:15.953
[Laios] Marcille!

08:17.371 --> 08:19.165
[gasps] How's Falin?

08:19.832 --> 08:21.083
Alive and well.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.212
-But she's still a bit disoriented.
-Huh?

08:26.672 --> 08:29.342
[Marcille whimpering]

08:29.425 --> 08:30.885
[Marcille] Falin!

08:32.428 --> 08:34.805
[sobs]

08:34.889 --> 08:36.599
[Marcille] I'm so glad!

08:36.682 --> 08:38.184
Thank goodness!

08:38.684 --> 08:40.436
-[sobs]
-[Falin] Marcille…

08:42.313 --> 08:43.606
Hm.

08:43.689 --> 08:45.650
-[Marcille sobbing]
-[approaching footsteps]

08:48.069 --> 08:49.487
[Falin] Chilchuck.

08:49.570 --> 08:50.988
[Chilchuck] How are you feeling?

08:52.073 --> 08:54.242
She's still kinda confused about this.

08:54.325 --> 08:56.369
Oh, right. This guy here?

08:56.452 --> 08:57.870
His name is Senshi.

08:57.954 --> 09:00.248
He's been a big help during our journey.

09:00.915 --> 09:02.667
Good to meet you, Falin.

09:02.750 --> 09:04.585
I've heard a lot about you.

09:05.169 --> 09:06.504
Senshi.

09:07.046 --> 09:09.423
-[stomach grumbles]
-[all] Hmm?

09:10.758 --> 09:12.843
[all chuckle]

09:12.927 --> 09:14.011
[Laios] Hm.

09:14.095 --> 09:16.889
Seems like a good time
to start prepping a meal.

09:18.516 --> 09:20.434
[water trickling]

09:20.518 --> 09:21.686
Thank goodness!

09:21.769 --> 09:23.688
I was so worried, Falin!

09:23.771 --> 09:26.774
I'm so happy
that everything worked out in the end!

09:26.857 --> 09:28.818
-Uh, Marcille?
-Hm?

09:28.901 --> 09:31.153
I can wash myself, you know.

09:31.237 --> 09:34.574
Yeah, but I wanted to make sure
your skin was properly restored.

09:34.657 --> 09:36.576
[Falin] That tickles!

09:37.159 --> 09:39.328
[Marcille] Yes. Good.

09:40.037 --> 09:42.915
[gasps] Why is there a bruise here?

09:42.999 --> 09:44.917
That's a mark I got from tripping

09:45.001 --> 09:47.587
and hitting the edge of the stairs
when I was a little kid.

09:47.670 --> 09:49.589
Oh, that's all?

09:50.298 --> 09:53.759
[Falin] Marcille,
you look even paler than I do.

09:53.843 --> 09:56.345
That's because I don't have any mana.

09:56.429 --> 09:59.557
If I eat something and get rest,
I should be fine--

10:00.433 --> 10:01.350
Huh?

10:03.686 --> 10:05.354
[yelps] What are you--

10:06.188 --> 10:09.609
Sorry if I scared you, I was trying
to give you some of my mana.

10:09.692 --> 10:11.152
You don't have to do that.

10:11.235 --> 10:14.614
I don't even think you have enough
to share with me right now, do you?

10:14.697 --> 10:16.574
[Falin] I actually feel good.

10:16.657 --> 10:20.202
Like there's power
welling deep inside of me.

10:21.203 --> 10:23.372
Falin, you're still on the mend,

10:23.456 --> 10:27.168
so please don't use magic
until you're used to your body again.

10:30.254 --> 10:32.173
[Falin] I died, didn't I?

10:34.050 --> 10:36.552
I don't really remember much about it.

10:37.428 --> 10:38.929
What happened exactly?

10:39.597 --> 10:41.474
You were all covered in wounds, and…

10:41.557 --> 10:44.268
for the Red Dragon to appear here…

10:44.352 --> 10:46.687
Wait! Are Shuro and Namari okay?

10:46.771 --> 10:48.022
I would feel just awful

10:48.105 --> 10:50.775
if anyone risked their lives
and got hurt because of me.

10:50.858 --> 10:52.068
No, they're all fine.

10:52.151 --> 10:53.277
-[Falin] Also…
-Uh?

10:53.361 --> 10:55.029
…that magic circle I saw…

10:56.614 --> 10:59.742
there was something
that just didn't feel right about it.

11:01.118 --> 11:02.578
I'm so sorry.

11:03.204 --> 11:06.082
It's all my fault
you had to use something like that.

11:08.125 --> 11:09.293
Stop worrying!

11:09.377 --> 11:10.795
Uh…

11:10.878 --> 11:14.757
Sure, we ran into some hardships,
things got pretty rough.

11:14.840 --> 11:17.551
But it's easy to look back
and laugh at all that now,

11:17.635 --> 11:19.804
'cause everything
turned out well in the end!

11:20.596 --> 11:23.808
Falin, there's no need for you
to blame yourself.

11:24.475 --> 11:27.144
[Marcille] No one regrets
anything that we've been through.

11:28.437 --> 11:29.605
Hm.

11:33.150 --> 11:37.321
[Marcille] As for that magic circle,
things will be fine if we erase it.

11:37.405 --> 11:38.823
[groans]

11:38.906 --> 11:40.825
-[Marcille] For the moment…
-Huh?

11:40.908 --> 11:44.078
…our biggest concern
is how to safely get back home.

11:44.161 --> 11:46.705
Oh! I still have to wash all my clothes.

11:46.789 --> 11:49.083
And we still have to find you
a new outfit.

11:49.166 --> 11:52.128
Ah, if it weren't for those stupid frogs.

11:52.211 --> 11:53.462
There were frogs?

11:55.297 --> 11:56.465
[Chilchuck] What do we do now?

11:57.383 --> 11:58.968
Return to the surface.

11:59.552 --> 12:02.430
[Laios] We can't use return magic
or the Orcs' tunnels,

12:02.513 --> 12:04.890
so we'll have to get to the castle
from the main road.

12:04.974 --> 12:06.225
[Chilchuck] Not what I meant.

12:06.308 --> 12:08.269
You may have rescued your sister,

12:08.352 --> 12:10.980
but the fact remains
that we're still broke.

12:11.063 --> 12:13.691
I do have some savings
in the bank, you know.

12:13.774 --> 12:15.818
But no promissory note.

12:15.901 --> 12:18.112
And it'll take a month to reproduce it.

12:18.195 --> 12:19.905
[Laios] Yeah, you're right.

12:21.740 --> 12:23.576
So about that Marcille,

12:23.659 --> 12:25.119
the black magic she used,

12:25.202 --> 12:27.163
did you already know she had that ability?

12:27.872 --> 12:29.832
I never asked her about the details,

12:29.915 --> 12:33.169
but she had mentioned
wanting to go into a dungeon to study it.

12:33.252 --> 12:35.004
[Chilchuck] It always seemed weird to me.

12:35.087 --> 12:37.548
An elf who looked like
she was living pretty comfy

12:37.631 --> 12:39.508
wanting to go into a dungeon?

12:39.592 --> 12:42.136
You don't suppose she's one
of those dark elves, do you?

12:42.219 --> 12:43.804
-[Laios] Oh?
-I don't want her causing

12:43.888 --> 12:45.764
any problems for us…

12:45.848 --> 12:48.893
-[Chilchuck gasps]
-Who are you calling a dark elf?

12:48.976 --> 12:50.227
[screams]

12:50.311 --> 12:53.147
If dark magic was harmless,
it wouldn't be forbidden!

12:53.230 --> 12:54.398
Oh, yeah?

12:54.482 --> 12:56.901
So you consider healing magic harmless?

12:57.485 --> 12:59.778
'Cause even that can be used for torture.

12:59.862 --> 13:03.407
I'm researching ways that forbidden magic
can be useful to people.

13:03.491 --> 13:06.160
And honestly, I'm not ashamed of it.

13:06.243 --> 13:07.411
[both] Uh…

13:07.495 --> 13:09.747
Although I think it's for the best
if we forget about

13:09.830 --> 13:12.583
the method of resurrection
this time around, if that's okay?

13:12.666 --> 13:15.044
Didn't you just say that
you weren't ashamed of it?

13:15.878 --> 13:17.421
[sighs] It's fine.

13:17.505 --> 13:18.964
It's all over anyway.

13:19.048 --> 13:21.425
Hm? I just realized…

13:22.092 --> 13:24.428
-[Senshi humming]
-Huh?

13:24.512 --> 13:27.431
[continues humming]

13:27.515 --> 13:28.933
[Laios] <i>Where did Senshi go?</i>

13:29.016 --> 13:30.809
Maybe dealing with the dragon meat?

13:30.893 --> 13:33.103
Oh, I just passed Mr. Senshi.

13:33.187 --> 13:35.856
He was carrying a giant pan
along with firewood.

13:35.940 --> 13:37.024
Like I said.

13:37.107 --> 13:38.317
He's prepping food.

13:39.276 --> 13:40.694
-[Laios] Hmm.
-Hm?

13:40.778 --> 13:42.446
Near the dragon?

13:43.697 --> 13:44.949
[both whimper]

13:45.032 --> 13:46.200
[all] We got to stop him!

13:46.283 --> 13:47.660
[Falin] What's happening?

13:47.743 --> 13:50.454
When I cut open the dragon,
I cut the fuel organ.

13:50.538 --> 13:52.373
[Laios] So lighting a fire
close to it is gonna…

13:52.915 --> 13:54.083
[gasps]

13:54.166 --> 13:55.334
Senshi!

13:55.417 --> 13:56.710
Please!

13:56.794 --> 13:58.963
-[Laios] Stop!
-[loud explosion]

13:59.046 --> 14:02.591
-[loud rumble]
-[all groan]

14:04.593 --> 14:06.387
[groans]

14:13.978 --> 14:15.354
-[coughs]
-He…

14:16.105 --> 14:17.147
He's alive.

14:17.231 --> 14:19.650
Is this defensive magic?

14:21.777 --> 14:23.654
[gasps softly]

14:24.238 --> 14:26.407
Falin, did you cast that?

14:26.490 --> 14:27.491
I think so.

14:27.575 --> 14:30.411
How'd you do it so fast
and without chanting?

14:31.412 --> 14:32.413
I don't know.

14:32.496 --> 14:35.916
[Falin] I thought about needing
to protect everyone, and then…

14:36.000 --> 14:37.001
Hmm.

14:37.084 --> 14:38.419
-[Chilchuck] That's amazing.
-Hm?

14:38.502 --> 14:40.546
Is it that sudden heroic strength thing?

14:41.213 --> 14:44.049
Sure had been real helpful to have
when we were fighting the Red Dragon.

14:44.133 --> 14:45.050
-Hm.
-[chuckles]

14:45.134 --> 14:47.595
[Marcille] Anyway,
you were revived not that long ago,

14:47.678 --> 14:50.556
so please,
refrain from using any more magic.

14:51.473 --> 14:52.933
That startled me.

14:53.017 --> 14:56.312
Didn't I say that dragons breathe fire
from fuel they produce?

14:56.937 --> 14:58.564
[Laios] You ignited that fuel.

14:59.064 --> 15:00.774
[Senshi] It's not going out, huh?

15:00.858 --> 15:02.985
[Laios] The fat inside
the body is burning.

15:03.068 --> 15:04.570
It'll die down eventually.

15:05.404 --> 15:08.157
If that's the case,
then I can't take the meat from in there.

15:08.741 --> 15:10.576
Hmm. Not good.

15:11.619 --> 15:13.037
[flame crackles]

15:13.829 --> 15:15.664
Guess I'll use that fire to cook.

15:16.165 --> 15:20.836
[Senshi] Mix flour, yeast, salt,
and water in a bowl, and knead well.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.588
Let it rest for a bit…

15:22.671 --> 15:24.089
Go take a bath while it rests.

15:25.299 --> 15:27.593
[Senshi] Shape it to your liking
as you stretch it out,

15:27.676 --> 15:29.595
and add your choice of toppings.

15:30.262 --> 15:33.098
Lightly sprinkle flour
onto a piece of dragon hide,

15:33.682 --> 15:36.101
then place it inside the dragon.

15:36.852 --> 15:38.854
Cut off the tip of the dragon's tail.

15:38.938 --> 15:40.856
No, that's so wasteful!

15:40.940 --> 15:43.859
Now, skin it and place it in a soup.

15:43.943 --> 15:45.861
Cut the meat into a block shape,

15:46.570 --> 15:49.990
place it on a heated scale,
and after both sides are seared,

15:50.074 --> 15:51.992
dip it into some seasoning.

15:54.995 --> 15:55.996
[both gulp]

15:56.080 --> 15:57.247
[Senshi] It's ready!

15:57.331 --> 15:58.540
DRAGON TAIL SOUP

15:58.624 --> 16:01.502
ONION PIZZA, ROAST RED DRAGON

16:01.585 --> 16:02.711
Oh, man.

16:02.795 --> 16:04.088
Looks delicious!

16:04.171 --> 16:05.005
Uh?

16:05.839 --> 16:06.799
Is this okay to eat?

16:06.882 --> 16:08.509
-Of course, it isn't!
-Of course, it isn't!

16:08.592 --> 16:09.760
[both gasp]

16:13.347 --> 16:14.765
Uh…

16:18.310 --> 16:19.269
Tasty!

16:19.353 --> 16:21.939
It feels like the first good meal
I've eaten in a while.

16:22.022 --> 16:23.023
Good, good!

16:23.107 --> 16:24.650
Take your revenge on that dragon.

16:24.733 --> 16:26.694
-[Marcille groans]
-I guess it's fine.

16:26.777 --> 16:28.821
I'm just glad that she's feeling better.

16:29.613 --> 16:32.533
[light music playing]

16:32.616 --> 16:35.327
Ah… [grunts]

16:37.413 --> 16:40.582
It's pretty tough,
but the flavor seems kind of familiar.

16:40.666 --> 16:43.002
Yeah, I can't really place it.

16:43.085 --> 16:45.045
I don't think it's cow or pig though.

16:45.129 --> 16:47.923
If anything, it kinda tastes like…

16:48.632 --> 16:50.759
It's a bit like Living Armor, isn't it?

16:50.843 --> 16:51.927
Ah, you think so?

16:52.011 --> 16:54.805
I don't taste
the same rusty tinge the armor had.

16:55.389 --> 16:57.391
[Chilchuck]
The Kelpie and frog were pretty soft.

16:57.474 --> 16:59.643
So maybe it's more like the Basilisk?

17:00.144 --> 17:02.062
[Marcille] What do you think, Laios?

17:04.940 --> 17:07.067
What are you all even talking about?

17:07.151 --> 17:08.318
[Laios] This color!

17:08.902 --> 17:10.070
This firm texture!

17:10.654 --> 17:11.822
The rich flavor!

17:11.905 --> 17:14.575
Each of these things
are distinctly unique!

17:14.658 --> 17:18.454
So, why do you keep comparing
the taste of this to anything else?

17:18.537 --> 17:22.207
Because this is the flavor of a dragon!

17:25.794 --> 17:26.879
Uh…

17:26.962 --> 17:28.756
[Marcille] Oh, uh, Falin?

17:28.839 --> 17:31.467
You may have realized by now, but…

17:31.550 --> 17:34.970
We haven't had the resources to buy food,
so we've been eating monsters.

17:35.054 --> 17:36.138
Ah!

17:37.097 --> 17:38.599
So cool.

17:38.682 --> 17:40.976
That is so cool!

17:41.060 --> 17:42.770
[Falin] What kind of monsters did you eat?

17:42.853 --> 17:44.938
And how did you eat them? Tell me!

17:45.022 --> 17:46.565
Worried for nothing.

17:46.648 --> 17:48.317
This is the worst possible outcome!

17:48.400 --> 17:51.487
-We ate a Scorpion and a Slime.
-[Falin gasps]

17:51.570 --> 17:52.863
Even a Walking Mushroom.

17:52.946 --> 17:54.782
-[Falin] No way! You did?
-[Laios snaps fingers]

17:54.865 --> 17:57.618
We harvested vegetables
from some Golems too.

17:57.701 --> 17:58.744
[Falin] Wow.

17:58.827 --> 18:00.454
You ate a Fish-man?

18:00.537 --> 18:02.748
That wasn't an option.

18:02.831 --> 18:04.625
We did eat some Living Armor though.

18:04.708 --> 18:06.752
[Falin] Huh? How'd you do that?

18:06.835 --> 18:10.672
Let's see.
The armor is basically the outer shell,

18:10.756 --> 18:13.300
and then,
inside is a mollusk colony, which--

18:13.383 --> 18:16.053
Wouldn't it be a lot faster
to show her the real thing?

18:16.136 --> 18:17.262
Uh…

18:19.098 --> 18:20.015
Huh?

18:20.099 --> 18:21.600
-What's this about?
-Shh!

18:24.228 --> 18:25.270
-Huh?
-Huh?

18:25.354 --> 18:27.272
[whimpers]

18:27.356 --> 18:29.691
Laios! Why'd you keep this from us?

18:29.775 --> 18:31.735
-I'm so sorry.
-Oh.

18:32.236 --> 18:34.404
Adorable. Can I touch?

18:35.823 --> 18:38.158
-[chitters]
-[Falin] Huh?

18:38.242 --> 18:39.785
It went back in.

18:41.662 --> 18:42.704
Huh?

18:43.413 --> 18:45.124
[Chilchuck] It moves around on its own.

18:45.207 --> 18:46.750
[Marcille] Seriously?

18:46.834 --> 18:47.668
[Laios] Sorry.

18:48.252 --> 18:51.797
It was only supposed to tide me over
until I found another weapon.

18:51.880 --> 18:54.424
But it reacts to other monsters,
which is convenient.

18:55.008 --> 18:57.219
You were oddly perceptive at times.

18:57.302 --> 18:59.638
[Chilchuck] We should've had Namari
appraise it for us.

18:59.721 --> 19:01.223
In that situation,

19:01.306 --> 19:03.809
I probably would have also thought
to hold on to it.

19:03.892 --> 19:05.561
But tell everyone next time.

19:05.644 --> 19:07.771
[Chilchuck] If you lose the trust
of those around you,

19:07.855 --> 19:09.398
you lose everything.

19:10.107 --> 19:11.358
I won't do it again.

19:11.441 --> 19:12.651
You have my word.

19:12.734 --> 19:14.570
[Chilchuck]
All right. So, what's your plan now?

19:14.653 --> 19:17.322
I'd like to keep it
until I get another weapon.

19:17.406 --> 19:20.492
[Laios] <i>I can kill it
if I submerge it in water.</i>

19:20.576 --> 19:22.161
<i>But I'd have to break the sword</i>

19:22.244 --> 19:24.288
<i>to get it out
or it would just rot in there.</i>

19:24.371 --> 19:25.455
[Marcille] <i>That's not good.</i>

19:25.539 --> 19:27.332
[Chilchuck] <i>Guess we'll keep an eye on it.</i>

19:27.416 --> 19:30.794
Aren't you the one who said
monsters are dangerous creatures?

19:31.420 --> 19:33.839
And trust me,
I haven't forgotten about that.

19:33.922 --> 19:35.841
I figured after I had made it harmless,

19:35.924 --> 19:38.844
I could just go on and use it
however I felt like.

19:38.927 --> 19:40.971
But I guess I was wrong.

19:41.054 --> 19:43.599
It's too difficult to use monsters
while they're still alive.

19:44.808 --> 19:46.768
What does it taste like, brother?

19:46.852 --> 19:48.103
Do you want to eat it?

19:48.187 --> 19:50.189
Yes, please! I'd love that!

19:50.272 --> 19:52.107
[Marcille groans]

19:56.486 --> 19:58.280
[Senshi] There's doors
all over this place,

19:58.363 --> 20:01.033
but seems like
only two of them lead outside, huh?

20:01.116 --> 20:02.868
[Laios] No getting ambushed at least.

20:05.704 --> 20:07.122
[Marcille] Hm.
[chuckles]

20:07.206 --> 20:10.125
This house seems like
it will be comfortable to live in.

20:10.209 --> 20:12.377
[Chilchuck]
Why do they have seven bathrooms, though?

20:12.461 --> 20:14.338
[Laios] All right. Let's sleep here then.

20:14.421 --> 20:17.883
[Marcille] Yay! It's been ages
since I slept on a real bed!

20:17.966 --> 20:19.176
[Chilchuck] We still got to use

20:19.259 --> 20:20.636
-our sleeping bags, you know.
-Huh?

20:27.809 --> 20:29.853
I'm sorry to be intruding like this.

20:30.520 --> 20:32.981
Once we get enough rest,
then we'll be on our way.

20:33.482 --> 20:34.900
Hey, what's up?

20:34.983 --> 20:36.526
[Falin] A resident.

20:36.610 --> 20:37.903
She's letting us stay.

20:38.487 --> 20:39.404
Is that so?

20:39.488 --> 20:40.656
[Laios] That's great.

20:41.990 --> 20:45.661
There are only four of 'em,
so we'll have to share a sleeping bag.

20:45.744 --> 20:49.373
We haven't really slept in the same bed
since our school days, have we?

20:49.456 --> 20:51.041
I wonder if we'll both fit.

20:51.792 --> 20:54.795
I feel like I've probably gotten
a lot taller since then, huh?

20:54.878 --> 20:57.256
[Marcille] Oh, don't be so ridiculous!

20:57.339 --> 20:59.049
-[giggles]
-[Falin gasps]

20:59.132 --> 21:02.678
I don't care if you've grown.
You're still a runt in my eyes.

21:02.761 --> 21:04.179
[Marcille giggles]

21:04.263 --> 21:05.430
Huh.

21:06.974 --> 21:09.184
I'm glad that you're with us again.

21:10.519 --> 21:11.770
Yeah. Me, too.

21:14.856 --> 21:17.442
I'm gonna go say goodnight to my brother.

21:20.028 --> 21:21.405
[Laios groaning]

21:21.488 --> 21:22.948
-[Falin] Brother?
-[Laios] Hmm?

21:23.615 --> 21:24.700
What is it?

21:26.785 --> 21:27.786
[grunts softly]

21:32.291 --> 21:33.834
This injury here…

21:33.917 --> 21:36.003
You were being reckless.

21:36.086 --> 21:36.962
Why would you do…

21:37.045 --> 21:41.216
Ah! [groans]

21:41.300 --> 21:44.553
Maybe if a certain sister of mine
hadn't been reckless first,

21:44.636 --> 21:46.805
I wouldn't have even had that injury.

21:46.888 --> 21:47.723
Huh?

21:47.806 --> 21:50.350
So don't ever do anything like that again!

21:50.434 --> 21:53.770
I honestly can't say
I even recall what I--

21:54.688 --> 21:59.359
[soft string music plays]

22:00.277 --> 22:01.778
[Falin] I won't do it again.

22:05.073 --> 22:07.492
Goodnight, big brother.

22:08.201 --> 22:09.995
You too. Sleep tight.

22:11.788 --> 22:13.040
Huh?

22:20.255 --> 22:22.132
[footsteps approaching]

22:31.892 --> 22:36.396
[foreboding music playing]

22:41.026 --> 22:44.029
[closing theme music playing]
